The agent mode (scripts/teamsolve/pipeline.py, task.py, failures.py, gitstate.py and the
agents-mode prompts in prompts.py) is adapted from Memdoor's built-in team-solve
(https://github.com/guregodevo/memdoor, workflows/team-solve at commit
47dad8b5ca3dcdeb559be8ff97f268762fb60980): its task template, planner, settle rules, check and
baseline semantics, failures parser, scope report, direct/ideate/solve/review/repair/judge
prompts and keep net. The sample-checker semantics, the sample problem (sample/) and the
parity-test scenarios in tests/test_team_solve.py are adapted from Memdoor's
examples/workflows/team-solve at commit 4b7ca6e239cbc777fe8135410cd6771414242713. Memdoor is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
Changes: the workflow engine and its bash/awk scripts were rewritten in Python; memdoor's run
folder and tools were replaced by this skill's (.team-solve/runs/<id>/, codex exec roles); the
single review/repair round became a loop of rounds with a fresh judge; tree states are git
trees through a private index (with a shadow repository outside git) instead of stash and
mtime scans; a failing Check that a baseline cannot explain counts as a failure instead of
turning the Check off; an --until end condition is carried into the Prompt and Done when; the
checker was ported from bash to Python and extended to functional (starter-code) samples.
